1
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:20,729
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

2
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:43,853
{\an8}DECEMBER 31

3
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:46,189
EPISODE 32
I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

4
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,191
Hmm...

5
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:50,193
Let's see here.

6
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:54,697
- Who are we waiting for?
- Grandpa, right?

7
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:57,659
<i>Our annual tradition,</i>

8
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:00,703
<i>playing cards with the TV on
in the background.</i>

9
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:04,040
<i>It's no different
from any other New Year's Eve.</i>

10
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:07,127
<i>Was it all just a dream?</i>

11
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:10,421
<i>Christmas Eve and us living together
under the same roof?</i>

12
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,843
<i>No, none of it was a dream.</i>

13
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:17,095
Did you not like it?

14
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:21,266
<i>And I still haven't
talked to her about it.</i>

15
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:24,978
Hmm... I'll pass.

16
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:27,355
Yes! I'm out.

17
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:30,316
<i>Mmm?</i>

18
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,777
<i>I'll text her
and wish her a happy New Year.</i>

19
00:02:33,444 --> 00:02:35,280
Oh, almost time!

20
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:38,408
<i>Six, five...</i>

21
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:42,495
- <i>And then...
-</i> ...<i>four, three, two, one.</i>

22
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:44,372
<i>Happy New Year!</i>

23
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:48,501
MOM
CHINATSU! HAPPY NEW YEAR!

24
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:51,462
Chinatsu is still in Nagano, right?

25
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:53,715
I hope she's enjoying
her family time there.

26
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:56,259
<i>Why did you have to text her first?</i>

27
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:58,261
DAD
HOW'S YOUR GRANDPA'S PLACE?

28
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:02,348
<i>Now that they texted her
in the group chat,</i>

29
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,392
<i>it feels awkward to text her privately.</i>

30
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,395
CHINATSU KANO
HAPPY NEW YEAR!

31
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,773
IT'S SNOWING HERE
SHOVELING IT HAS BEEN GOOD EXERCISE...

32
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:13,276
<i>Even this far away,</i>

33
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,196
<i>she still makes my heart race.</i>

34
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:20,325
NISHIDA SENPAI
LET'S GO TO THE SHRINE!!!

35
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,411
TACHIBANA SHRINE ENTRANCE

36
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:28,917
He's here!

37
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,419
You're late again, Taiki!

38
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:34,422
Well, I couldn't find my scarf.

39
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:36,674
Hi, Karen, it's been a while.

40
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:38,384
Looks like you've gotten taller.

41
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:40,261
- Huh?
- You think so?

42
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:42,347
You see him every day, remember?

43
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:46,768
He just seems more manly to me.

44
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:49,812
Uh, thank you, I guess.

45
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:51,981
Hmm?

46
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:54,651
Come on, hurry up! Let's get our pray on!

47
00:03:59,906 --> 00:04:03,076
Uh, hey, hold on a second.
I need something to drink.

48
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:07,497
I'll treat you.

49
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:09,457
Wait, why?

50
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:12,961
'Cause my younger siblings
loved the cookies

51
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:14,462
you gave us for Christmas.

52
00:04:14,545 --> 00:04:15,546
Uh...

53
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,217
Mmm?

54
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:24,222
{\an8}<i>OSHIRUKO</i> DRINK

55
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:35,316
- There are so many people here.
- Feels like we're barely moving.

56
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:49,998
<i>Health, club activities,
love, studies, world peace.</i>

57
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,000
<i>And, please,</i>

58
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:55,962
<i>let this be the year I let nothing stop me
from reaching my goals.</i>

59
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:02,176
Let's see what my fortune says, my dudes!

60
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:04,387
{\an8}BAD LUCK

61
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,139
{\an8}Bad Luck?

62
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:08,933
I'll keep drawing
until I get a Great Blessing!

63
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:12,020
- Uh, is that allowed?
- I'd always heard it was fine.

64
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:13,521
Hmm?

65
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:14,689
{\an8}GREAT MISFORTUNE

66
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:19,027
{\an8}Great Misfortune?

67
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:21,321
I have to draw a Great Blessing!

68
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:22,530
Hmm.

69
00:05:22,613 --> 00:05:24,532
<i>Second time, Blessing.</i>

70
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:27,535
<i>Third time, Future Blessing.</i>

71
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:29,037
<i>Fourth time...</i>

72
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,039
{\an8}GREAT BLESSING

73
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:33,041
<i>...Great Blessing!</i>

74
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:42,550
<i>"Regarding love, don't hesitate."</i>

75
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:45,303
Uh...

76
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:46,721
TACHIBANA SHRINE

77
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:47,805
Hey, hey.

78
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:49,557
What does your fortune say, Hina-bean?

79
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,060
{\an8}Ta-da!

80
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,478
{\an8}Whoa!

81
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:54,562
{\an8}What'd you get?

82
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:58,066
Well, I'm only interested
in the love section, so...

83
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:01,569
"Regarding love,
a thorny path lies ahead"?

84
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:04,822
I'm drawing again!

85
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,577
Great Blessing!

86
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:12,288
- Looks like everyone's happy now.
- Yeah, that's so much better.

87
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:13,581
All right, squad.

88
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:17,585
The time has come to hit the food stalls!

89
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:20,088
<i>Amazake!</i>

90
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:22,090
Just try not to get lost.

91
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:29,305
Huh?

92
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,599
Is something wrong?

93
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:34,268
It kinda looked like
you were limping a little.

94
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:37,855
Actually, someone in the crowd
stepped on my foot earlier.

95
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,149
I think it got scraped up.

96
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,526
I have bandages.

97
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:43,861
Let's go over there for a sec
and put one on.

98
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,613
Huh? But everyone else is...

99
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:47,490
Uh?

100
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:49,992
Moriya, would you mind

101
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,578
telling everyone
we'll catch up with them later?

102
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:53,496
Oh.

103
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,249
Sure, you got it.

104
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,341
<i>Huh? I lost them.</i>

105
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:07,677
Typical upperclassmen.

106
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:11,013
Always blazing forward
without ever looking back to check for us.

107
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:13,724
<i>I'll try texting them.</i>

108
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:17,645
{\an8}INOMATA FAMILY
SOMEONE SENT A STICKER

109
00:07:20,731 --> 00:07:21,858
{\an8}KAREN MORIYA
INCOMING CALL

110
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:25,403
{\an8}Hi, Chii. Happy New Year!

111
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:29,323
{\an8}<i>You can't just video call someone
without warning them first.</i>

112
00:07:30,074 --> 00:07:33,953
I thought it would be nice to give you
my New Year's greeting face-to-face.

113
00:07:34,036 --> 00:07:36,664
The whole group is out for <i>hatsumode.</i>

114
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:38,958
See for yourself.

115
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:45,256
Oh, yeah.

116
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,216
We lost Taiki a while ago.

117
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:50,470
<i>I wanted the two of them
to say hi, though.</i>

118
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:55,224
{\an8}Did you guys get a fortune and stuff?

119
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:56,767
<i>Oh, did we ever!</i>

120
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:57,852
TAIKI
NEW MESSAGE

121
00:07:57,935 --> 00:08:00,480
Hmm? Are you texting someone?

122
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:02,440
If you're busy, I can call you back--

123
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:12,700
{\an8}TAIKI INOMATA
CAN WE TALK WHEN YOU GET BACK?

124
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:15,745
{\an8}I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

125
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:18,873
{\an8}READ 1:42 A.M.

126
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,324
{\an8}CHINATSU KANO
SURE

127
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,493
Uh...

128
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:19,058
A-ha, there's our boy now.

129
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:22,812
You've got some nerve getting lost
after showing up late.

130
00:09:22,895 --> 00:09:24,063
I'm sorry, guys.

131
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:27,275
You better not be late
for our ski trip on the 4th.

132
00:09:27,358 --> 00:09:29,569
I'll set 20 alarms that morning.

133
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:32,446
Uh, where are Kyo and Hina?

134
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:37,243
Hmm? Did you both get lost too?

135
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:39,704
Nuh-uh, we were just doing our own thing.

136
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:42,164
What a bunch of individual-sport athletes.

137
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:43,583
So true.

138
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:46,335
They say "like attracts like," you know?

139
00:09:46,419 --> 00:09:47,587
I'm like you now?

140
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,297
Mmm...

141
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:53,968
- See you at practice!
- Bye, guys!

142
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:04,103
I can't believe you can be the manager
of such a free-spirited team.

143
00:10:04,186 --> 00:10:05,605
Impressive, right?

144
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:08,441
You're actually really caring.

145
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:10,234
What do you mean, "actually"?

146
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:12,069
It's just you're the type to go all-in

147
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:13,863
for the wrong guy. So be careful.

148
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:16,115
Don't worry, I'm well aware.

149
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:19,619
You know, that four-eyes
might be a good match for you.

150
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:22,246
Kasahara?

151
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:23,914
But don't you like him?

152
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:27,126
You looked so jealous
when he came back with Hina.

153
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:29,378
No, I'm not jealous at all!

154
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:31,422
My type is more handsome boys.

155
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:34,050
Handsome face, handsome hair,
handsome everything.

156
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:35,134
MY NO. 1 LOVE
YUSA

157
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:37,136
'Kay.

158
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:40,264
<i>Maybe I looked so bothered...</i>

159
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:43,142
<i>because I knew how Hina-bean felt.</i>

160
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:46,145
<i>Kasahara is probably...</i>

161
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:50,524
Me into him? Not a chance.

162
00:10:51,108 --> 00:10:52,026
Sure.

163
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:54,779
Whatever you say.

164
00:11:00,117 --> 00:11:04,038
{\an8}JANUARY 1

165
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:07,041
HAPPY NEW YEAR

166
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:10,044
- That looks delicious. Yeah.
- Turned out pretty good, right?

167
00:11:10,836 --> 00:11:11,837
Welcome!

168
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:14,632
- That road has gotten nicer.
- Here you go.

169
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:15,549
- Thank you.
- I know.

170
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:17,051
{\an8}JANUARY 2

171
00:11:17,134 --> 00:11:18,552
{\an8}Let's fly them over the river!

172
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:19,470
{\an8}- Wait up!
- Yeah!

173
00:11:19,553 --> 00:11:21,055
{\an8}There's open space over there!

174
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:23,808
{\an8}- Bet I can fly it higher than you!
- No way!

175
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:28,062
{\an8}4TH: JYO-OU UNIVERSITY YOSHIKUNI HAYAMA
HIROSHIMA AKISEIRYU HIGH

176
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:37,571
<i>Time is going by so slowly.</i>

177
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:45,121
<i>Chinatsu isn't coming back until the 6th.</i>

178
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:48,582
<i>I'm going skiing with the badminton team
on the 4th and 5th,</i>

179
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,668
<i>but that still leaves four days.</i>

180
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:54,088
<i>I wanna see her.</i>

181
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,798
{\an8}CAN WE TALK WHEN YOU GET BACK?

182
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:57,091
{\an8}I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

183
00:11:57,174 --> 00:11:58,175
Mmm...

184
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:01,804
<i>Actually, maybe I don't.</i>

185
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,682
<i>'Cause when I do, I'll have to...</i>

186
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,523
I'm going for a run.

187
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:17,403
Goodness, he can't even take a break
during the holidays?

188
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,530
That's just how he is.

189
00:13:10,581 --> 00:13:12,124
<i>At this point a year ago,</i>

190
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:15,252
<i>she and I hadn't even had
a real conversation.</i>

191
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:19,089
<i>But before I knew it...</i>

192
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:44,031
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

193
00:14:17,648 --> 00:14:19,358
<i>Hey! Morning, Taiki!</i>

194
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:39,795
Hello, I'm back!

195
00:14:42,047 --> 00:14:43,674
New Year's cards!

196
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:46,385
I left the ones
that we got today over there.

197
00:14:46,468 --> 00:14:47,678
Huh?

198
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:51,682
TO TAIKI INOMATA

199
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:00,190
UNZEN, NAGANO
CHINATSU KANO

200
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:06,864
{\an8}<i>"Happy New Year to you all!"</i>

201
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:08,824
{\an8}<i>"Thanks to the whole Inomata family,</i>

202
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,034
{\an8}<i>I didn't have to move</i>

203
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:13,203
{\an8}<i>and was able to stay
at the same school last year."</i>

204
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,334
<i>Oh, man.</i>

205
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:23,923
<i>I want to see her.</i>

206
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:28,177
{\an8}<i>Just her handwriting
makes me feel that way.</i>

207
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:30,596
<i>Even when she's not here,</i>

208
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,932
<i>I can't help thinking about her.</i>

209
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:37,728
<i>Just sensing her presence makes me happy.</i>

210
00:15:39,772 --> 00:15:41,065
<i>That's the kind of love</i>

211
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,275
<i>I'm feeling right now.</i>

212
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:46,737
{\an8}JANUARY 1, NAGANO

213
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,977
{\an8}TAIKI
CAN WE TALK WHEN YOU GET BACK?

214
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,269
{\an8}I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

215
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:36,787
How late are you going to sleep in?

216
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:39,081
I'm getting up now!

217
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,710
Good morning.

218
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,545
Oh, good morning, Chii.

219
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:46,839
What do you feel like
having on your <i>mochi?</i>

220
00:16:46,922 --> 00:16:48,716
Red bean paste? Soy sauce?

221
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:51,552
Don't rush her
before she's had a chance to sit down.

222
00:16:56,473 --> 00:16:57,558
Thank you for the meal.

223
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:06,316
That soup is loaded with tons of veggies
I grew right here myself.

224
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:13,574
You're really packing it in there, Chii.

225
00:17:13,657 --> 00:17:15,659
'Cause it's delicious.

226
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:18,078
Hey, has anybody seen Dad?

227
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:20,581
He went around to say hi to the neighbors.

228
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:23,083
He hasn't been home in ages, you know?

229
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:26,754
Why don't you tell your old grandpa
about your life?

230
00:17:26,837 --> 00:17:28,714
How's basketball going?

231
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:29,798
Studies good?

232
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,801
Everything's going fine.

233
00:17:33,343 --> 00:17:35,929
Got a boyfriend?

234
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:37,222
Honey...

235
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:40,851
Kids these days don't like
being asked questions like that.

236
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:43,812
- C'mon, aren't you curious?
- Oh, dear.

237
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,650
How'd you two meet again?

238
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:51,737
If I remember correctly,
it was at Grandma's work, right?

239
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:54,073
<i>Yes, at the inn.</i>

240
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:58,494
<i>Grandpa came by every morning
to supply them with fresh vegetables.</i>

241
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:00,913
And when did you know
you were in love with Grandma?

242
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:06,251
Grandpas these days don't like being asked
questions like that either.

243
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:09,379
- Mmm.
- How convenient for you.

244
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:12,758
I forgot. It was so long ago.

245
00:18:12,841 --> 00:18:15,427
Don't listen to him, he's just being shy.

246
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:19,890
- Chinatsu.
- Mmm.

247
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:22,518
When you're done,
we'll shovel the snow, okay?

248
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:23,602
Okay.

249
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:29,399
{\an8}JANUARY 2

250
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,923
I'm gonna take a little walk.

251
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:55,134
Walking in this cold weather?

252
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:58,929
She's always finding some way
to stay active, that girl.

253
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,403
It's chilly outside today, huh?

254
00:19:14,486 --> 00:19:16,572
I told you to wear more layers.

255
00:19:16,655 --> 00:19:20,075
You were right.

256
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:22,161
- Are you okay?
- Well, I don't wanna go back yet.

257
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,954
You'll catch a cold.

258
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:45,142
I can't believe it. Look at all this snow!

259
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:48,896
Let's have a snowball fight!

260
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:51,899
I get a free shot.

261
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:52,983
What?

262
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:22,179
If you'd like, you can wear my scarf!

263
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:28,268
You keep yourself warm.

264
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:30,187
<i>Taiki Inomata.</i>

265
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:44,201
You're so disciplined,
training early every morning.

266
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:08,392
Good morning.

267
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:19,027
<i>He's early again today.</i>

268
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:21,530
<i>Taiki's here again.</i>

269
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,032
<i>And again.</i>

270
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:39,006
Oh, Chii, about earlier...

271
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:40,549
I will tell you

272
00:21:41,216 --> 00:21:43,510
as long as it stays between us.

273
00:21:43,593 --> 00:21:45,053
What were we talking about?

274
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:46,888
The words your grandpa said

275
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:48,974
when he confessed his love for me.

276
00:21:51,184 --> 00:21:56,440
{\an8}JANUARY 3

277
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:09,995
He walked right up to me,
looking so shy, and said...

278
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,084
<i>"Every morning,</i>

279
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:18,879
<i>I catch myself</i>

280
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:21,673
<i>wanting to see you."</i>

